(5741103, 835492, 108580, '<td valign="top">Interesting shot, unique. Looks like Cola :) Nice splash effect. Unusual B and W PP. Higher marks also for effort in research and OOB title.<br/> <br/>Useless info of the day:<br/>Chromite is a mineral, not a liquid as you no doubt know. Once it is smelted/leeched, it is in ''liquid'' form but then its glowing gold in colour and is primarily used in the making of (stainless) steel. The biggest single producer is South Africa @ 44% of global output (6.5 Million Metric Tons per year). The closest mines are less than 2 hours drive from me in the enormous <a href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:BIC00.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Bushveld Igneous Complex</a>.</td>', 'Interesting shot, unique. Looks like Cola :) Nice splash effect. Unusual B and W PP. Higher marks also for effort in research and OOB title. Useless info of the day:Chromite is a mineral, not a liquid as you no doubt know. Once it is smelted/leeched, it is in ''liquid'' form but then its glowing gold in colour and is primarily used in the making of (stainless) steel. The biggest single producer is South Africa @ 44% of global output (6.5 Million Metric Tons per year). The closest mines are less than 2 hours drive from me in the enormous Bushveld Igneous Complex.', '2009-11-25 04:44:39.000000', NULL, 1),
