(5742165, 834678, 10523, '<td valign="top">good idea, nice shot</td>', 'good idea, nice shot', '2009-11-25 20:25:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(5742189, 835389, 10785, '<td valign="top">With the broken bulb and the lit candle, this photo represents de-evolution to me. (Just an fyi about the message communicated and how it can be interpreted.) From a photographic standpoint, the photo looks very well lit and if you took it from just the ambient light created by the candle, it is very well done!</td>', 'With the broken bulb and the lit candle, this photo represents de-evolution to me. (Just an fyi about the message communicated and how it can be interpreted.) From a photographic standpoint, the photo looks very well lit and if you took it from just the ambient light created by the candle, it is very well done!', '2009-11-25 20:41:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(5742242, 834547, 10785, '<td valign="top">This is a good landscape photo. The content is a very worthy subject. You have all the great features of a well composed landscape... the shrubs in the foreground, the buildling occupying the midground and the mountains and sky in the middle.<br/> <br/>There are a few things that I can see to improve this. I would take a look at the aperture setting. The foreground appears blurred. I am not sure if it from camera shake or from the f-stop chosen. Second, there is a definite line through the middle of the photo. It is the line that separates the base of the mountain from the foreground. I would use the rule of thirds and either increase or decrease the amount of foreground to change where that line hits. You might want to try to recompose this by changing the camera height from the ground or changing the angle of view. One last thing would be to try a polarizing filter. That would help with the haze that appears in the background. All in all this shot made me think about the techniques used and that is a great thing. My critiques were more for my own self improvement but I hope they were helpful for you as well.</td>', 'This is a good landscape photo. The content is a very worthy subject. You have all the great features of a well composed landscape... the shrubs in the foreground, the buildling occupying the midground and the mountains and sky in the middle. There are a few things that I can see to improve this. I would take a look at the aperture setting. The foreground appears blurred. I am not sure if it from camera shake or from the f-stop chosen. Second, there is a definite line through the middle of the photo. It is the line that separates the base of the mountain from the foreground. I would use the rule of thirds and either increase or decrease the amount of foreground to change where that line hits. You might want to try to recompose this by changing the camera height from the ground or changing the angle of view. One last thing would be to try a polarizing filter. That would help with the haze that appears in the background. All in all this shot made me think about the techniques used and that is a great thing. My critiques were more for my own self improvement but I hope they were helpful for you as well.', '2009-11-25 21:11:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(5742245, 835246, 10785, '<td valign="top">Good concept and subject. I really like the composition here. I think this could improve by using a polarizing filter to cut the glare from the water. I like how you combined a bug and a leaf in the shot. Sorta serendipitous.</td>', 'Good concept and subject. I really like the composition here. I think this could improve by using a polarizing filter to cut the glare from the water. I like how you combined a bug and a leaf in the shot. Sorta serendipitous.', '2009-11-25 21:14:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(5742302, 835036, 111474, '<td valign="top">Interesting idea. I am very supprised that the focus is so soft, with the amount of light you are dealing with. I would be adding other light''s so you don''t over expose the eliment.</td>', 'Interesting idea. I am very supprised that the focus is so soft, with the amount of light you are dealing with. I would be adding other light''s so you don''t over expose the eliment.', '2009-11-25 22:11:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(5742304, 835452, 111474, '<td valign="top">It looks like there is quite a bit of motion blur.</td>', 'It looks like there is quite a bit of motion blur.', '2009-11-25 22:12:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(5742312, 834857, 111474, '<td valign="top">Clever idea. I would have liked to see more of the tools a greater DoF (and they need a clean). The lighting on the orange is nice, but quite flat on the tools.</td>', 'Clever idea. I would have liked to see more of the tools a greater DoF (and they need a clean). The lighting on the orange is nice, but quite flat on the tools.', '2009-11-25 22:21:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(5742316, 834309, 111474, '<td valign="top">Nice capture. The loss of focus around the right edge and not the left makes the central composition odd. You may want to look at cropping this so you only see the blue sky as the background and the stem is in the left 1/3.</td>', 'Nice capture. The loss of focus around the right edge and not the left makes the central composition odd. You may want to look at cropping this so you only see the blue sky as the background and the stem is in the left 1/3.', '2009-11-25 22:26:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(5742319, 835246, 111474, '<td valign="top">Very soft focus. You may also find a polerising filter is useful to remove the reflections.</td>', 'Very soft focus. You may also find a polerising filter is useful to remove the reflections.', '2009-11-25 22:28:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(5742324, 834678, 58610, '<td valign="top">Good one!</td>', 'Good one!', '2009-11-25 22:31:01.000000', NULL, 1),
