(5751965, 834360, 9114, '<td valign="top">You are my hero Lydia and I''m so sorry you are hurting now. Congratulations on the red<br/> <br/>You are, ARE so lucky to have had a parent like that. Not all of us do. I weep with you<br/> <br/>Debbi</td>', 'You are my hero Lydia and I''m so sorry you are hurting now. Congratulations on the red You are, ARE so lucky to have had a parent like that. Not all of us do. I weep with you Debbi', '2009-12-03 09:18:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(5752094, 835286, 96751, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your posthumous yellow!!!  Glad to see I was not the only one who thought it was a nail in a tree :-)  This is my kind of shot - love to try and figure out what it is.</td>', 'Congrats on your posthumous yellow!!!  Glad to see I was not the only one who thought it was a nail in a tree :-)  This is my kind of shot - love to try and figure out what it is.', '2009-12-03 10:40:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(5752130, 835235, 67237, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the ribbon!. This was my pick for the blue for execution and creativity.<br/>I just realized the score is the same as the red ribbon winner. What is the rule to determine the order in these cases?</td>', 'Congrats on the ribbon!. This was my pick for the blue for execution and creativity.I just realized the score is the same as the red ribbon winner. What is the rule to determine the order in these cases?', '2009-12-03 11:14:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(5752140, 834787, 107922, '<td valign="top">I won''t say I understand it (I Googled, too) and I''m sorry it didn''t do well in the challenge.  I *will* say that I think it''s a marvelous image that I drooled over while it was in voting.  With those wonderful colors &amp; great sense of movement, it would look fabulous printed large.</td>', 'I won''t say I understand it (I Googled, too) and I''m sorry it didn''t do well in the challenge.  I *will* say that I think it''s a marvelous image that I drooled over while it was in voting.  With those wonderful colors & great sense of movement, it would look fabulous printed large.', '2009-12-03 11:19:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(5752191, 834787, 108580, '<td valign="top">Just goes to show how fickle voters can be even with G**gle at their fingertips...<br/>I didn''t think it was worth 10 for DPC but not 1,2,3,4 or 5 either! <br/>Zur Farbenlehre contains some of the earliest and most accurate descriptions of phenomena such as coloured shadows, refraction, and chromatic aberration.<br/>Keep up the good and thought provoking work.</td>', 'Just goes to show how fickle voters can be even with G**gle at their fingertips...I didn''t think it was worth 10 for DPC but not 1,2,3,4 or 5 either! Zur Farbenlehre contains some of the earliest and most accurate descriptions of phenomena such as coloured shadows, refraction, and chromatic aberration.Keep up the good and thought provoking work.', '2009-12-03 12:18:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(5752268, 834360, 24454, '<td valign="top">Lydia!  At first I was smiling, like always, at your adorable frog pictures, then I wanted to cry as I read about your loss of your dad. I am so sorry! I saw your picture on Facebook, but I didn''t realize that your loss was so fresh!  I''m so thankful that you are the kind of daughter you are (and so not surprised), and that your relationship was filled with so much love.<br/> <br/>I''ve lost both of my parents, so I understand your hurt very well.  I loved what you said about "his body dying".  What a testament to your faith that the soul lives on, and you <i>will</i> be reunited again one day!</td>', 'Lydia!  At first I was smiling, like always, at your adorable frog pictures, then I wanted to cry as I read about your loss of your dad. I am so sorry! I saw your picture on Facebook, but I didn''t realize that your loss was so fresh!  I''m so thankful that you are the kind of daughter you are (and so not surprised), and that your relationship was filled with so much love. I''ve lost both of my parents, so I understand your hurt very well.  I loved what you said about "his body dying".  What a testament to your faith that the soul lives on, and you will be reunited again one day!', '2009-12-03 13:03:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(5752389, 834360, 86090, '<td valign="top">ohh Lydia, at first I was happy to seeing you on the first page again, but now I''m in tears. It''s always difficult to lose somebody, and all that we have left, are the sweet memories of them, my heart goes to you and your family, and I''m glad, you got to be part of the life of such a wonderful man. Hugs.</td>', 'ohh Lydia, at first I was happy to seeing you on the first page again, but now I''m in tears. It''s always difficult to lose somebody, and all that we have left, are the sweet memories of them, my heart goes to you and your family, and I''m glad, you got to be part of the life of such a wonderful man. Hugs.', '2009-12-03 13:53:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(5753037, 834360, 98771, '<td valign="top">Lydia, not very often am I at a loss for words, this is one of those rare occasions. First let me say how sorry I am to hear of your loss, and it sounds as if he was a wonderful man. Secondly, congratulations on the ribbon, it''s a wonderful shot, and like your father, the title made me chuckle.</td>', 'Lydia, not very often am I at a loss for words, this is one of those rare occasions. First let me say how sorry I am to hear of your loss, and it sounds as if he was a wonderful man. Secondly, congratulations on the ribbon, it''s a wonderful shot, and like your father, the title made me chuckle.', '2009-12-03 20:52:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(5753041, 834678, 98771, '<td valign="top">Wonderful, congratulations!</td>', 'Wonderful, congratulations!', '2009-12-03 20:53:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(5753050, 835235, 98771, '<td valign="top">I''m awestruck, this is an excellent image. Well done and congratulations.</td>', 'I''m awestruck, this is an excellent image. Well done and congratulations.', '2009-12-03 20:54:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5753263, 835235, 97814, '<td valign="top">Wow!  Congratulations again Brad!  You are such an amazing photographer!</td>', 'Wow!  Congratulations again Brad!  You are such an amazing photographer!', '2009-12-03 22:43:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(5753522, 834787, 19936, '<td valign="top">Learn something new every day.  Thanks.</td>', 'Learn something new every day.  Thanks.', '2009-12-04 01:02:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5753551, 834678, 97166, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jjstager2:</b></div><hr/><i> I marvel at the four geniuses who scored this a "1" </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Had I voted this challenge, I would have given it a 1. For me, this kind of photograph exemplifies all that I find wrong with the voting populace of DPC. It is nothing more than a water drop on a needle point against a piece of paper with letters written on it.  It has no real composition, it has no real substance, it has no real feeling. Yet it, and shots like it, repeatedly make ribbon lists. Why? because the voters are brain-dead sheep on a mass scale.<br/> <br/>So yes, I would have given it a 1 myself, and I wonder why more didn''t, actually.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by jjstager2: I marvel at the four geniuses who scored this a "1"   Had I voted this challenge, I would have given it a 1. For me, this kind of photograph exemplifies all that I find wrong with the voting populace of DPC. It is nothing more than a water drop on a needle point against a piece of paper with letters written on it.  It has no real composition, it has no real substance, it has no real feeling. Yet it, and shots like it, repeatedly make ribbon lists. Why? because the voters are brain-dead sheep on a mass scale. So yes, I would have given it a 1 myself, and I wonder why more didn''t, actually. ', '2009-12-04 02:08:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(5753582, 834360, 18655, '<td valign="top">This is priceless Lydia! I just don''t understand how a boring waterdroplet could beat your score. Congrats!<br/> <br/>I''m sorry to hear about your dad. Great picture of you two!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-12-04 03:59:09.</i></td>', 'This is priceless Lydia! I just don''t understand how a boring waterdroplet could beat your score. Congrats! I''m sorry to hear about your dad. Great picture of you two!', '2009-12-04 02:52:25.000000', '2009-12-04 03:59:09.000000', 0),
(5753600, 834729, 93384, '<td valign="top">I love it! The chain helps make the dog seem aggressive. Scary, great colors!</td>', 'I love it! The chain helps make the dog seem aggressive. Scary, great colors!', '2009-12-04 03:28:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(5753722, 834360, 28427, '<td valign="top">My sincerest condolences.<br/> <br/>Congrats on the red ribbon.  B.t.w.: nice picture of you and your dad. He will be with you forever and will live on in the heart and mind of his beloved ones.</td>', 'My sincerest condolences. Congrats on the red ribbon.  B.t.w.: nice picture of you and your dad. He will be with you forever and will live on in the heart and mind of his beloved ones.', '2009-12-04 07:11:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5754089, 834360, 67027, '<td valign="top">My condolences, i know how you feel, my Dad died aged 50 when I was 20, 16 years ago.<br/> <br/>The last words he said to me were "See you later"  - same thing, not ill, massive heart attack.<br/> <br/>You are absolutely right when you say to tell people how you feel.  You may not get another chance xx</td>', 'My condolences, i know how you feel, my Dad died aged 50 when I was 20, 16 years ago. The last words he said to me were "See you later"  - same thing, not ill, massive heart attack. You are absolutely right when you say to tell people how you feel.  You may not get another chance xx', '2009-12-04 11:15:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(5754671, 834360, 43463, '<td valign="top">I love the humor is this shot! Congrats on your ribbon.<br/> <br/>My condolences on the loss of your Dad, Lydia. In the very least the lasting memory you will carry in your heart was his love for you and the laugh you gave him with this photo.<br/> <br/>And I take the advice you give to heart - no one in my family leaves the house at the start of the day without me telling them I love them - tis been that way for quite some time now:-)</td>', 'I love the humor is this shot! Congrats on your ribbon. My condolences on the loss of your Dad, Lydia. In the very least the lasting memory you will carry in your heart was his love for you and the laugh you gave him with this photo. And I take the advice you give to heart - no one in my family leaves the house at the start of the day without me telling them I love them - tis been that way for quite some time now:-)', '2009-12-04 16:31:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(5754694, 835235, 108544, '<td valign="top">Great execution with painted light! Congrats on the great finish!</td>', 'Great execution with painted light! Congrats on the great finish!', '2009-12-04 17:10:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(5754695, 834360, 14476, '<td valign="top">Oh, Lydia - your sweet and charming image brings a smile to my face, and your story below it brings tears. <br/> <br/>My thoughts are with you.</td>', 'Oh, Lydia - your sweet and charming image brings a smile to my face, and your story below it brings tears.  My thoughts are with you.', '2009-12-04 17:11:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(5754796, 834678, 43156, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by K10DGuy:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jjstager2:</b></div><hr/><i> I marvel at the four geniuses who scored this a "1" </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Had I voted this challenge, I would have given it a 1. For me, this kind of photograph exemplifies all that I find wrong with the voting populace of DPC. It is nothing more than a water drop on a needle point against a piece of paper with letters written on it.  It has no real composition, it has no real substance, it has no real feeling. Yet it, and shots like it, repeatedly make ribbon lists. Why? because the voters are brain-dead sheep on a mass scale.<br/> <br/>So yes, I would have given it a 1 myself, and I wonder why more didn''t, actually. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You have the right for your own opinion, but I find your comment offensive and unfair to the author of this image and all other DPC members.</td>', 'Originally posted by K10DGuy: Originally posted by jjstager2: I marvel at the four geniuses who scored this a "1"   Had I voted this challenge, I would have given it a 1. For me, this kind of photograph exemplifies all that I find wrong with the voting populace of DPC. It is nothing more than a water drop on a needle point against a piece of paper with letters written on it.  It has no real composition, it has no real substance, it has no real feeling. Yet it, and shots like it, repeatedly make ribbon lists. Why? because the voters are brain-dead sheep on a mass scale. So yes, I would have given it a 1 myself, and I wonder why more didn''t, actually.   You have the right for your own opinion, but I find your comment offensive and unfair to the author of this image and all other DPC members.', '2009-12-04 19:43:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(5755204, 835457, 90495, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Yo_Spiff:</b></div><hr/><i> You got robbed. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I agree. Wonderfully photographed.</td>', 'Originally posted by Yo_Spiff: You got robbed.   I agree. Wonderfully photographed.', '2009-12-05 00:47:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(5755205, 834729, 90495, '<td valign="top">Cool image.</td>', 'Cool image.', '2009-12-05 00:49:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(5755208, 835406, 108580, '<td valign="top">Hi, you did well to get 6 comments. I have a really good scoring entry right now and I have only 3 comments... DPC is wierd. The comments are worth more to me than the 1,2,3 voters however... :)<br/>I like your shot and idea of writing music as a science but think it was too underexposed and the shadows and lost in space background for more than a 5.</td>', 'Hi, you did well to get 6 comments. I have a really good scoring entry right now and I have only 3 comments... DPC is wierd. The comments are worth more to me than the 1,2,3 voters however... :)I like your shot and idea of writing music as a science but think it was too underexposed and the shadows and lost in space background for more than a 5.', '2009-12-05 00:56:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(5755745, 835296, 99506, '<td valign="top">Hey Elle I was browsing through a book and came across "Coleman''s Cafe" by William Christenberry and it reminded me very much of your entry here.<br/> <br/>//huntermuseum.org/gallery/60/christenberry/colemans-caf-greensboro-alabama-1971/?sortBy=artist_lastname&amp;perPage=36k<br/> <br/></td>', 'Hey Elle I was browsing through a book and came across "Coleman''s Cafe" by William Christenberry and it reminded me very much of your entry here. //huntermuseum.org/gallery/60/christenberry/colemans-caf-greensboro-alabama-1971/?sortBy=artist_lastname&perPage=36k ', '2009-12-05 12:18:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(5755780, 835457, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>My thoughts on the image:</b> Nice combination of interesting elements that cover both sides of this ''argument'' between science and religion.  I like the left-to-right flow that you created with the books, but overall, the image is a bit to dark for my personal taste.<br/> <br/><b>My ideas for improvement:</b> I think that this one would have made a stronger entry with a little more exposure, as well as a black and white conversion.  I''d also like to see the cloth underneath your subjects the same black color as your background.<br/> <br/><b>Where I would have/did score this entry:</b> I did not vote in this particular challenge, but I would tend to agree with the voters here.  I would have most likely scored this one in the 5 range, perhaps 6 because I do like the subject matter.  I think that a black and white conversion would have given this one a little more pop.<br/> <br/>Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,<br/><b>Eric</b> <br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  My thoughts on the image: Nice combination of interesting elements that cover both sides of this ''argument'' between science and religion.  I like the left-to-right flow that you created with the books, but overall, the image is a bit to dark for my personal taste. My ideas for improvement: I think that this one would have made a stronger entry with a little more exposure, as well as a black and white conversion.  I''d also like to see the cloth underneath your subjects the same black color as your background. Where I would have/did score this entry: I did not vote in this particular challenge, but I would tend to agree with the voters here.  I would have most likely scored this one in the 5 range, perhaps 6 because I do like the subject matter.  I think that a black and white conversion would have given this one a little more pop. Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,Eric ', '2009-12-05 13:11:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(5756494, 835235, 98022, '<td valign="top">Great shot Brad. Congrats on getting bumped up to a red ribbon!</td>', 'Great shot Brad. Congrats on getting bumped up to a red ribbon!', '2009-12-06 03:31:19.000000', NULL, 0),
