(5756687, 835405, 100773, '<td valign="top">It''s a shame that some voters (me as well in this and many other cases) doesn''t quite get the full extent of the photo until after the voting has ended. This is a great photo. I''m glad I wasn''t to harsh on you. Gratulations on making it to your top 5 on your profile ;)</td>', 'It''s a shame that some voters (me as well in this and many other cases) doesn''t quite get the full extent of the photo until after the voting has ended. This is a great photo. I''m glad I wasn''t to harsh on you. Gratulations on making it to your top 5 on your profile ;)', '2009-12-06 11:29:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(5757437, 834678, 97559, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by K10DGuy:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jjstager2:</b></div><hr/><i> I marvel at the four geniuses who scored this a "1" </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Had I voted this challenge, I would have given it a 1. For me, this kind of photograph exemplifies all that I find wrong with the voting populace of DPC. It is nothing more than a water drop on a needle point against a piece of paper with letters written on it.  It has no real composition, it has no real substance, it has no real feeling. Yet it, and shots like it, repeatedly make ribbon lists. Why? because the voters are brain-dead sheep on a mass scale.<br/> <br/>So yes, I would have given it a 1 myself, and I wonder why more didn''t, actually. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>AMEN!  I couldn''t have said it better myself.  I left this one-dimensional, parochial, insipid site for all of the reasons you state.</td>', 'Originally posted by K10DGuy: Originally posted by jjstager2: I marvel at the four geniuses who scored this a "1"   Had I voted this challenge, I would have given it a 1. For me, this kind of photograph exemplifies all that I find wrong with the voting populace of DPC. It is nothing more than a water drop on a needle point against a piece of paper with letters written on it.  It has no real composition, it has no real substance, it has no real feeling. Yet it, and shots like it, repeatedly make ribbon lists. Why? because the voters are brain-dead sheep on a mass scale. So yes, I would have given it a 1 myself, and I wonder why more didn''t, actually.   AMEN!  I couldn''t have said it better myself.  I left this one-dimensional, parochial, insipid site for all of the reasons you state.', '2009-12-06 22:52:38.000000', NULL, 0),
